Greg Olivera wrote:
> Playing around with the protection racket I've run into 2 problems: Pets
> finding level teleports, and trapdoors.  What do you do when you're too weak
> to handle the level you're on, but your pet is suddenly not with you?

If my pet left through level teleport and if the pet is necessary
for my survival then I go down one level and then up until the
upmost dungeon level immediately to see whether I can find him. I
usually don't bother any more finding my pet below level 15 or 20.

In former times I had more problems with falling through trapdoors
myself. A typical event sequence for level changes was like that:
trapdoor 5->8, climb up to 7, trapdoor 7->9, trapdoor 9->10, etc.
Problems like that can be smoothen when you immediately go down
a stair whenever you find one (and up again, of course). If you
fall down you'll see the upstairs of that level immediately and
have no need for thorough search (which might lead to another
trapdoor event). That's especially helpful in dark levels and open
levels like the mines which usually require exhaustive search.

To your last question I'd say: then don't descend too early! And
don't completely rely on your pet(s); build up alternatives.

If you find yourself in a hopeless situation just because one of
the options vanished that you relied upon then you haven't had
enough options. Try to get a bit more paranoid. ;-)

